# Firmware policy and configuration headers

`firmware_config.h` validates the compile-time Wi-Fi, device identity/secret,
backend origin, and root CA supplied by the ignored `secrets.h` file.
`secrets.example.h` is the tracked template. Changing configuration requires a
new firmware build and reflash; the application has no persistent credential
store or local recovery service.

Fleet confidentiality depends on the `esp32dev-secure` Secure Boot V2 and
release-mode flash-encryption gate. See `../README.md`,
`../../docs/hardware/HARDWARE_TELEMETRY.md`, and
`../../docs/operations/HARDWARE_SECURITY_PROVISIONING.md`.
